      hoy: [
        'Sixteen advantage claims tracked. Three still standing. Six eroded.',
        'No third party has ever reproduced another team’s headline result from its published artifacts.',
        'Of the 78 sealed runs with a verdict, 43 went to the classical champion, 6 tied, and 4 went to the quantum arm. We published the aggregate anyway: pooled properly, the quantum contribution was not significant. Picking the four would have been the vendor’s move.',
        'That is a reason to wait, and a reason to know exactly when to stop waiting.',
      ],
      queH: 'What we do',
      que: 'We keep the record. Every claim dated, sourced, statused and linked to its seal — including the ones we published against ourselves. When something in your industry changes, you will see it in the registry before you see it in a keynote.',
      recibesH: 'What you get',
      recibes: 'Full access to the Evidence Library: the index, the search, the claims, the evidence levels, the survival clock. Exports with seals, watchlists with alerts, and the full weekly.',
      muestra: 'Browsing is free. Look before you pay →',
      precioH: 'Price',
      precio: 'Evidence Library — Analyst, US$149 per seat / month.',
      precio2: 'Firm — US$1,900 per month for up to 15 seats, with a quarterly briefing and shared watchlists. Fifteen Analyst seats would cost US$2,235. Evidence levels are identical in every tier: what you pay for is depth of tooling, never a different truth.',
      ledgerH: 'From the ledger, for you',
      ledger: 'Five claims in the registry have no challenge on record. Two of them are ours, and one of those is a negative we published against ourselves.',
